Random Number Generator Analysis

Aim

To evaluate operating-system random-number generation mechanisms and investigate their suitability for cryptographic applications.

Methods

Linux /dev/urandom

OpenSSL rand

.NET RandomNumberGenerator API on Linux

Analysis

The Python analysis program evaluates:

Byte-frequency distribution

Bit distribution

Repeated four-byte patterns

Lag-1 serial correlation

Runs test

Files

src/: Source code and project configuration.

results/: Statistical results and graphs.

requirements.txt: Python dependencies.

Important Note

Statistical tests can identify certain deviations from randomness, but passing these tests does not prove cryptographic security. The .NET experiment was executed on Linux, not Windows CNG.
